From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omer Dangoor <omerdn1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:45:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ios): give each CLI session a free runner port instead of
 22087

maestro record, hierarchy and query pass the root --driver-host-port to
MaestroSessionManager, and without it an iOS session used the fixed port
22087. Two of them on different simulators at the same time therefore met
on one port. The runner token makes the second fail with "port taken".
Without the token, the second would have driven the first one's simulator.

Without --driver-host-port, an iOS session now binds a loopback socket to
port 0 and uses the port the OS assigns, as maestro test's selectPort and
the MCP server's per-session ports already do. A port the caller passes is
still used as is. Android is unchanged: its driver port, 7001, is a port on
the device, which Maestro opens through the adb transport of that device's
serial, so no host port is shared.

A second process on a simulator that another CLI session is using no
longer reaches that session's runner on the shared port. It starts its own
runner, as maestro test already does.
